# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots exim with dc_local_interfaces='0.0.0.0' (listening on
# every interface) in the background and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the SMTP daemon is ALREADY LISTENING on 0.0.0.0:25 when the agent starts,
#     which is what makes the "restricted the config but never restarted exim"
#     case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting exim cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART exim after editing
# update-exim4.conf.conf; exim reads dc_local_interfaces only at startup, so an
# un-restarted daemon keeps its 0.0.0.0 binding and verify.sh (which reads
# /proc/net/tcp) still FAILS.
